Package: thresholdopt
Type: Package
Title: Optimal Threshold for the Overlap of Two Ranked Gene Lists
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("João C. D.", "Muzzi", email = "j.muzzi@neuraxis.digital",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Mauro A. A.", "Castro", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimates the cut-off at which two independently ranked feature
    lists agree most strongly, instead of imposing an arbitrary one. Every
    candidate set size is evaluated: the overlap between the two top-n sets is
    scored with a hypergeometric tail probability computed in log space, and
    the score is regularised by the divergence between the lists so that the
    optimum is attained at neither extreme of the sweep. Returns the optimal
    threshold, the consensus feature set and the diagnostic figure of the
    source publication. Implements the method of Muzzi et al. (2025)
    <doi:10.1093/ejendo/lvaf138>.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
